<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodemir (Visigoth)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 743</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodemir was a Visigothic noble who governed south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> at the time of the Muslim conquest. After resisting the invaders he agreed the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orihuela">Orihuela</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-aziz-ibn-musa">Abd al-Aziz ibn Musa</a> in 713, keeping control of seven towns in return for tribute. His land became known to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> as Tudmir, after his name, and survived as an autonomous Christian district for several decades.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodemir-visigoth.jpg" alt="Theodemir (Visigoth)" width="183" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roxanna · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teodomiro_de_Orihuela.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
